<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="ZEC" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Fri Feb 12 2021 13:10:40 GMT-0600 (Central Standard Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Zechariah
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Zechariah
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Zechariah
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Zec
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Zechariah

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ZEC 1"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:1"/>In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, the word of Yahweh came to Zechariah, son of Berechiah, son of Iddo, the prophet, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 1:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:2"/>“Yahweh was angry {with} anger toward your fathers.
<verse eid="ZEC 1:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:3"/>And you shall say to them, ‘Thus says Yahweh of Armies, “Return to me”—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—“and I will return to you”, says Yahweh of Armies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:4"/>“Do not be like your fathers, to whom the former prophets called out, saying, ‘Thus says Yahweh of Armies, “Turn now from your evil ways and your evil deeds.”’ But they did not hear, and they did not pay attention to me”—the declaration of Yahweh.

<verse eid="ZEC 1:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:5"/>“Your fathers, where {are} they? And the prophets, do they live forever?

<verse eid="ZEC 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:6"/>But my words and my statutes, which I commanded my servants the prophets, did they not overtake your fathers? And they returned and said, ‘Just as Yahweh of Armies planned to do to us, according to our ways and according to our deeds, thus he has done with us.’”’”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:7"/>On the twenty-fourth day of the eleventh month, which {is} the month of Shebat, in the second year of Darius, the word of Yahweh came to Zechariah, son of Berechiah, son of Iddo, the prophet, saying:

<verse eid="ZEC 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:8"/>I saw in the night, and behold, a man riding on a red horse, and he was standing among the myrtle trees that {are} in the deep valley, and behind him
{were} red, reddish-brown, and white horses.

<verse eid="ZEC 1:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:9"/>And I said, “What {are} these, my lord?” And the angel who was speaking with me said to me, “I will show you what these {are}.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:10"/>And the man who was standing among the myrtle trees answered and said, “These {are} the ones whom Yahweh has sent to walk about in the earth.”

<verse eid="ZEC 1:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:11"/>And they answered the angel of Yahweh who was standing among the myrtle trees, and they said, “We have walked about in the earth, and behold, all of the earth is sitting and is at rest.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:12"/>And the angel of Yahweh answered and said, “Yahweh of Armies, until when will you not have compassion on Jerusalem and on the cities of Judah, with which you have been indignant these 70 years?”
<verse eid="ZEC 1:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:13"/>And Yahweh answered the angel who was speaking with me {with} good words, words of comfort.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:14"/>And the angel who was speaking with me said to me, “Call out, saying, ‘Thus says Yahweh of Armies, “I have been jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion {with} a great jealousy.

<verse eid="ZEC 1:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:15"/>And {with} a great anger I, I am angry with the nations that {are} at ease, for I, I was angry {only} a little, but they helped toward the evil.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:16"/>Therefore, thus says Yahweh, “I have returned to Jerusalem with compassions. My house will be built in her”—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—“and a measuring line will be stretched out over Jerusalem.”’

<verse eid="ZEC 1:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:17"/>Again, call out, saying, ‘Thus says Yahweh of Armies, “My cities will again overflow from goodness, and Yahweh will again comfort Zion, and he will again choose Jerusalem.”’”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:17"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:18"/>And I lifted up my eyes and I saw, and behold, four horns.

<verse eid="ZEC 1:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:19"/>And I said to the angel who was speaking with me, “What {are} these?” And he said to me, “These
{are} the horns that scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 1:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:20"/>And Yahweh showed me four craftsmen.

<verse eid="ZEC 1:20"/><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ZEC 1:21"/>And I said, “What
{are} these coming to do?” And he said, “These
{are} the horns that scattered Judah, according to the mouth of a man {who} has not lifted up his head. And these have come to terrify them, to cast down the horns of the nations, the ones lifting up a horn against the land of Judah to scatter her.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 1:21"/><verse eid="ZEC 1:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ZEC 2"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:1"/>And I lifted up my eyes and saw, and behold, a man, and in his hand {was} a rope of measuring.
<verse eid="ZEC 2:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:2"/>And I said, “Where are you going?” And he said to me, “To measure Jerusalem, to see what
{is} its width and what
{is} its length.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 2:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:3"/>And behold, the angel who was speaking with me was going out, and another angel was going out to meet him.
<verse eid="ZEC 2:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:4"/>And he said to him, “Run, speak to that young man, saying, ‘Jerusalem will be inhabited {as} open areas because of the multitude of man and beast in her midst. <verse eid="ZEC 2:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:5"/>And I, I will be for her—the declaration of Yahweh—a wall of fire all around, and for glory I will be in her midst.’”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:6"/>“Woe! Woe! Flee from the land of the north”—the declaration of Yahweh—“for as the four winds of the heavens, I have spread you out”—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="ZEC 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:7"/> <verse eid="ZEC 2:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:8"/>For thus says Yahweh of Armies—after glory he has sent me to the nations that are plundering you—for the one touching you is touching the apple of his eye. <verse eid="ZEC 2:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:9"/>“For behold, I am waving my hand over them, and they will be plunder for their slaves.” And you will know that Yahweh of Armies has sent me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:10"/>“Sing and rejoice, daughter of Zion, for behold, I am coming, and I will dwell in your midst”—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="ZEC 2:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:11"/>“And many nations will join themselves to Yahweh in that day, and they will be to me for a people, and I will dwell in your midst.” And you will know that Yahweh of Armies has sent me to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 2:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:12"/>And Yahweh will inherit Judah {as} his portion on the land of holiness, and he will again choose Jerusalem.
<verse eid="ZEC 2:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 2:13"/>Hush, all flesh, from the face of Yahweh, for he has been roused from the dwelling place of his holiness!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 2:13"/><verse eid="ZEC 2:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ZEC 3"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:1"/>And he made me see Joshua the high priest standing to the face of the angel of Yahweh, and the adversary standing on his right to accuse him.
<verse eid="ZEC 3:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:2"/>And Yahweh said to the adversary, “May Yahweh rebuke you, the adversary, and may Yahweh who is choosing Jerusalem rebuke you. {Is} this not a firebrand rescued from the fire?”
<verse eid="ZEC 3:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:3"/>And Joshua was clothed {in} filthy garments and standing to the face of the angel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:4"/>And he answered and said to the ones standing to the face of him, saying, “Remove the filthy garments from upon him.” And he said to him, “See, I have caused your iniquity to pass away from you, and I will clothe you {with} fine clothing.”
<verse eid="ZEC 3:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:5"/>And I said, “Let them set a clean turban on his head.” And they set the clean turban on his head and clothed him {with} garments, and the angel of Yahweh was standing {by.}

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:6"/>And the angel of Yahweh solemnly charged Joshua, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 3:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:7"/>“Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘If you will walk in my ways, and if you will keep my charge, then you also will judge my house and also will keep my courts, and I will give to you access among these who are standing {here.}

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 3:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:8"/>Hear now, Joshua the high priest, you and your companions who are sitting to the face of you, for they
{are} men of a sign, for behold, I am bringing my servant, the Branch.
<verse eid="ZEC 3:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:9"/>For behold, the stone that I have set to the face of Joshua, on one stone {are} seven eyes. Behold, I am engraving its engraving’—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—‘and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 3:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 3:10"/>In that day’—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—‘you will call, each man to his neighbor, to under {his} vine and to under {his} fig tree.’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 3:10"/><verse eid="ZEC 3:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ZEC 4"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:1"/>And the angel who was speaking with me returned and roused me like a man who is roused from his sleep.
<verse eid="ZEC 4:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:2"/>And he said to me, “What are you seeing?” And I said, “I have seen, and behold, a lampstand of gold, all of it, and its bowl on its top, and seven lamps on it, seven and seven tubes for the lamps that {are} on its top.
<verse eid="ZEC 4:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:3"/>And two olive trees {are} beside it, one on the right of the bowl and one on its left.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:4"/>And I answered and said to the angel who was speaking with me, saying, “What {are} these, my lord?”
<verse eid="ZEC 4:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:5"/>And the angel who was speaking with me answered and said to me, “Do you not know what these are?” And I said, “No, my lord.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:6"/>And he answered and said to me, saying, “This {is} the word of Yahweh to Zerubbabel, saying, ‘Not by might and not by power, but by my Spirit,’ says Yahweh of Armies.
<verse eid="ZEC 4:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:7"/>Who {are} you, great mountain, to the face of Zerubbabel? {You} will become a plain! And he will bring out the top stone {with} shouts of ‘Grace, grace to it!’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:8"/>And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 4:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:9"/>‘The hands of Zerubbabel have founded this house, and his hands will complete it.’ And you will know that Yahweh of Armies has sent me to you.

<verse eid="ZEC 4:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:10"/>For who has despised the day of small things? And they will rejoice and will see the stone of tin in the hand of Zerubbabel. These seven are the eyes of Yahweh; they are roaming through all of the earth.”

<verse eid="ZEC 4:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:11"/>And I answered and said to him, “What are these two olive trees on the right of the lampstand and on its left?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 4:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:12"/>And I answered a second time and said to him, “What
{are} the two branches of the olives that
{are} beside the two pipes of gold that are emptying the gold from upon them?”
<verse eid="ZEC 4:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:13"/>And he said to me, saying, “Do you not know what these are?” And I said, “No, my lord.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 4:13"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 4:14"/>And he said, “These are the two sons of the fresh oil, the ones standing before the Lord of all of the earth.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 4:14"/><verse eid="ZEC 4:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ZEC 5"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:1"/>And I turned and I lifted up my eyes and I saw, and behold, a flying scroll.
<verse eid="ZEC 5:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:2"/>And he said to me, “What are you seeing?” And I said, “I am seeing a flying scroll. Its length is 20 cubits and its width is ten cubits.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 5:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:3"/>And he said to me, “This
{is} the curse that is going out over the face of all of the earth, for everyone who is stealing from this
{side,} according to it, has been cleared, and everyone who is swearing from this
{side,} according to it, has been cleared.
<verse eid="ZEC 5:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:4"/>I have brought it out”—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—“and it will come to the house of the thief and to the house of the one swearing by my name to falsehood. And it will spend the night in the midst of his house and will consume it, and its timbers, and its stones.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:5"/>And the angel who was speaking with me went out, and he said to me, “Lift up now your eyes and see what this
{is} that is going out.”
<verse eid="ZEC 5:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:6"/>And I said, “What
{is} it?” And he said, “This
{is} the ephah that is going out.” And he said, “This
{is} their eye in all of the earth.”
<verse eid="ZEC 5:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:7"/>And behold, a disk of lead was being lifted up, and this
{was} one woman sitting in the midst of the ephah.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 5:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:8"/>And he said, “This
{is} the wickedness.” And he threw her into the midst of the ephah, and he threw the stone of lead to its mouth.

<verse eid="ZEC 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:9"/>And I lifted up my eyes and I saw, and behold, two women were going out, and wind
{was} in their wings. And they had wings like the wings of the stork. And they lifted up the ephah between the earth and between the heavens.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 5:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:10"/>And I said to the angel who was speaking with me, “Where are they taking the ephah?”
<verse eid="ZEC 5:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 5:11"/>And he said to me, “To build for her a house in the land of Shinar. And it will be established, and she will be set down there on her base.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 5:11"/><verse eid="ZEC 5:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ZEC 6"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:1"/>And I turned and I lifted my eyes and I saw, and behold, four chariots coming out from between two mountains. And the mountains {were} mountains of bronze.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:2"/>In the first chariot {were} red horses, and in the second chariot {were} black horses,
<verse eid="ZEC 6:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:3"/>and in the third chariot {were} white horses, and in the fourth chariot {were} spotted, strong horses.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:4"/>And I answered and said to the angel who was speaking with me,
“What are these, my lord?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:5"/>And the angel answered and said to me,
“These are the four winds of the heavens going out from standing before the Lord of all the earth.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:6"/>The
{chariot} in which {are} the black horses is going out to the land of the north, and the white ones went out after them, and the spotted ones went out to the land of the south.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:7"/>And the strong ones went out and sought to go to walk about in the earth. And he said,
“Go, walk about in the earth.” And they walked about in the earth.

<verse eid="ZEC 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:8"/>And he called out to me and spoke to me, saying,
“See, the ones going out to the land of the north have caused my spirit to rest in the land of the north.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:9"/>And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 6:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:10"/>“Take from the exiles—from Heldai, and from Tobijah, and from Jedaiah—and you, you shall come on that day, and you shall come to the house of Josiah, the son of Zephaniah, who have come from Babylon.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:11"/>And you shall take silver and gold, and you shall make crowns, and you shall set
{them} on the head of Joshua, the son of Jehozadak, the high priest.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 6:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:12"/>And you shall speak to him, saying, ‘Thus says Yahweh of Armies, saying, Behold, a man—Branch is his name—and from his place he will sprout, and he will build the temple of Yahweh.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:13"/>And he, he will build the temple of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he, he will bear glory,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will sit and rule on his throne.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And he will be a priest on his throne,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a counsel of peace will be between the two of them.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 6:13"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:14"/>And the crowns will be for Helem and for Tobijah and for Jedaiah and for Hen, the son of Zephaniah, as a memorial in the temple of Yahweh.
<verse eid="ZEC 6:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 6:15"/>And those far off will come and build in the temple of Yahweh, and you will know that Yahweh of Armies has sent me to you. And
{this} will happen if listening, you will listen to the voice of Yahweh your God.”


<verse eid="ZEC 6:15"/><verse eid="ZEC 6:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ZEC 7"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:1"/>And it happened in the fourth year of Darius the king, the word of Yahweh came to Zechariah, on the fourth {day} of the ninth month, in Kislev.
<verse eid="ZEC 7:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:2"/>Bethel had sent Sharezer and Regem-Melech and his men {to} beg before the face of Yahweh,
<verse eid="ZEC 7:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:3"/>saying to the priests who {were} at the house of Yahweh of Armies, {and} to the prophets saying, “Should I mourn in the fifth month by means of a fast, as I have done these many years?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:4"/>And it happened {that} the word of Yahweh of Armies came to me, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 7:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:5"/>“Speak to all the people of the land and to the priests and say, ‘When you fasted and mourned in the fifth and in the seventh {month} for these seventy years, were you fasting, fasting for me?
<verse eid="ZEC 7:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:6"/>When you ate and when you drank, did you not eat and drink for yourselves?
<verse eid="ZEC 7:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:7"/>Were these not the words that Yahweh proclaimed by the hand of the former prophets, when you still inhabited Jerusalem and the surrounding cities in prosperity and were settled in the Negev and the foothills to the west?’”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:8"/>The word of Yahweh came to Zechariah, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 7:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:9"/>“Thus says Yahweh of Armies saying, ‘Judge with true justice, and covenant faithfulness, and mercy. Let each man do this for his brother.
<verse eid="ZEC 7:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:10"/>And the widow and orphan, the foreigner, and the poor person—do not oppress them, and let a man not plot evil {against} his brother in your heart.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 7:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:11"/>But they refused to heed and gave a stubborn shoulder. Their ears were heavy from hearing.
<verse eid="ZEC 7:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:12"/>They made their heart as rock {to keep} from hearing the law and the words that Yahweh of Armies had sent by his Spirit by the hand of the former prophets. And great rage came from Yahweh of Armies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 7:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:13"/>‘It happened that as when he called, and they did not listen, so when they call, I will not listen,’ says Yahweh of Armies.
<verse eid="ZEC 7:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 7:14"/>‘And I scattered them with a whirlwind to all the nations that they had not known, and the land was made desolate after them from anyone passing through or returning. And they had made the land of desire into a wasteland.’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 7:14"/><verse eid="ZEC 7:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ZEC 8"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:1"/>And the word of Yahweh of Armies came, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 8:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:2"/>“Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘I have been jealous for Zion {with} a great jealousy, and I have been jealous for her {with} great heat.’
<verse eid="ZEC 8:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:3"/>Thus says Yahweh, ‘I will return to Zion and will live in the midst of Jerusalem, and Jerusalem will be called “the city of faithfulness” and the mountain of Yahweh of Armies, “the mountain of holiness!”’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:4"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘Old men and old women will again sit in the open areas of Jerusalem, and a man {with} his staff in his hand from a multitude of days.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:5"/>And the open areas of the city will be filled {with}  boys and girls playing in its open areas.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:6"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘If it is wonderful in the eyes of the remnant of this people in those days, will it also be wonderful in my eyes?’—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:7"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘Behold, I am saving my people from the land of the sunrise and from the land of the setting of the sun.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:8"/>And I will bring them, and they will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem, and they will be to me as a people, and I, I will be to them as God in faithfulness and in righteousness.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:9"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘May your hands be strong, you who are hearing in these days these words from the mouth of the prophets who {were} there on the day {when} the house of Yahweh of Armies was founded, the temple to be built.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:10"/>For to the face of those days, the wages of man were not, and the wages of the beast, there were none. And for the one going out and for the one coming in there was no peace from the enemy, and I sent every man, each against his neighbor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:11"/>But now, I will not be to the remnant of this people like the former days’—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:12"/>‘For {there} will be the seed of peace: the vine will give its fruit, and the land will give its produce, and the heavens will give their dew. And I will cause the remnant of this people to inherit all these things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:13"/>And it will be just as you were a curse in the nations, house of Judah and house of Israel, so I will save you and you will be a blessing. Do not fear; let your hands be strong!’

<verse eid="ZEC 8:13"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:14"/>For thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘Just as I planned to cause harm to you when your fathers angered me’—says Yahweh of Armies—‘and did not relent,
<verse eid="ZEC 8:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:15"/>thus I have turned; I plan in these days to cause good to Jerusalem and the house of Judah! Do not fear!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:16"/>These are the things that you must do: Speak truth, each with his neighbor; judge in your gates {with} faithfulness and a judgement of peace.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:17"/>And a man shall not plan evil within his heart {against} his neighbor, and oath of falseness you shall not love—for all of these {are that} which I hate!’—the declaration of Yahweh.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:17"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:18"/>And the word of Yahweh of Armies came to me, saying,
<verse eid="ZEC 8:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:19"/>“Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘The fast of the fourth, and the fast of the fifth, and the fast of the seventh, and the fast of the tenth {months} will become into joy, and into gladness, and into happy festivals for the house of Judah! And love faithfulness and peace!’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:20"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘Yet {it will happen} that nations and the inhabitants of many cities will come.
<verse eid="ZEC 8:20"/><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:21"/>The inhabitants of one {city} will go to another saying, “Let us quickly go to beg the face of Yahweh and to seek Yahweh of Armies! I, I also will go”
<verse eid="ZEC 8:21"/><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:22"/>Many people and mighty nations will come to seek Yahweh of Armies in Jerusalem and beg the face of Yahweh!’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 8:22"/><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ZEC 8:23"/>Thus says Yahweh of Armies, ‘In those days {there will be} ten men from every language of the nations who will grab, and they will grab the hem of a man of Judah, saying, “Let us go with you, for we have heard God is with you!”’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 8:23"/><verse eid="ZEC 8:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ZEC 9"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:1"/>The burden of the word of Yahweh in the land of Hadrach,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Damascus, his resting place;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for toward Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">are the eye of mankind and all of the tribes of Israel.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:2"/>And also Hamath borders on it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Tyre and Sidon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they are very wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:3"/>And Tyre has built herself a stronghold
</para>
  <para style="q2">and heaped up silver like dust,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and refined gold like the mud of the streets.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:4"/>Behold! The Lord will dispossess her
</para>
  <para style="q2">and strike down her wealth on the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and she, she will be devoured by fire.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:5"/>Ashkelon will see and be afraid;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Gaza, and it will writhe greatly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Ekron, for her hope has dried up!
</para>
  <para style="q1">And the king will perish from Gaza,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Ashkelon will not be inhabited!
<verse eid="ZEC 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:6"/>And a mixed people will dwell in Ashdod,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:7"/>And I will remove his blood from his mouth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his abominations from between his teeth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he also will be left behind for our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will be like a clan in Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Ekron, like a Jebusite.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:8"/>And I will camp around my house
</para>
  <para style="q2">as a guard against the one passing through and against the one returning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and no oppressor will pass over them again,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for now I have seen with my eyes!

<verse eid="ZEC 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:9"/>Rejoice greatly, daughter of Zion!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Shout, daughter of Jerusalem!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Behold! Your king is coming to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">righteous and being saved is he,
</para>
  <para style="q2">humble and riding on a donkey,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on a colt, the son of female donkeys.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:10"/>And I will cut off the chariot from Ephraim,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the horse from Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the bow of war will be cut off.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And he will speak peace to the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his dominion will be from sea to sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from the River to the ends of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:11"/>{As for} you also, by the blood of your covenant
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have set free your prisoners from the pit in which there is no water.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:12"/>Return to the stronghold, prisoners of hope!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even today I am declaring that I will return double to you,
<verse eid="ZEC 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:13"/>for I have bent for myself Judah, a bow;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have filled Ephraim.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will rouse your sons, Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">against your sons, Greece,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will make you like the sword of a mighty man.

<verse eid="ZEC 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:14"/>And Yahweh will appear over them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his arrow will go out like the lightning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the Lord Yahweh will blow on the shofar
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will go with the storms of the south.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:15"/>Yahweh of Armies will defend them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will devour and will subdue
</para>
  <para style="q2">the stones of the sling,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will drink and roar as with wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will be full like the bowl,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like the corners of the altar.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 9:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:16"/>And Yahweh their God will save them on that day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like the flock of his people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for they are the stones of a crown
</para>
  <para style="q2">gleaming over his land.
<verse eid="ZEC 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ZEC 9:17"/>For how {is} his goodness, and how {is} his beauty!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Grain the young men,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and new wine will make the virgins flourish.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 9:17"/><verse eid="ZEC 9:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ZEC 10"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:1"/>Ask for rain from Yahweh in the time of the spring rain,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, the one making thunderstorms,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he gives them rain showers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to a man, vegetation in the field.
<verse eid="ZEC 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:2"/>For household idols speak iniquity, and the diviners envision a lie,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they speak dreams of emptiness; with vanity they comfort.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Therefore, they journey like a flock;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are afflicted because there is no shepherd.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:3"/>“Against the shepherds my nose burns,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the male goats I will attend.
</para>
  <para style="q1">For Yahweh of Armies attends to his flock, the house of Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will make them like a horse of his splendor in the battle!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:4"/>From him a cornerstone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from him a {tent} peg,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from him a bow of war,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from him will come forth every ruler together.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Many modern versions put the idea of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">together</char> at the start of the next verse.</note>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:5"/>And they will be like warriors
</para>
  <para style="q2">trampling  in the mud of the streets in the battle,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will fight, for Yahweh is with them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will put to shame the riders of horses.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:6"/>And I will strengthen the house of Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will save the house of Joseph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will bring them back, for I have compassion on them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will be as though I had not rejected them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I am Yahweh their God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will answer them.
<verse eid="ZEC 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:7"/>And Ephraim will be like a warrior,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their heart will be glad as {with} wine,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their sons will see and rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their heart will exult in Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:8"/>I will whistle for them and gather them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I have redeemed them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will be many,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as they were many.
<verse eid="ZEC 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:9"/>And I will sow them among the peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the distant places they will remember me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will live with their sons and return.
<verse eid="ZEC 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:10"/>And I will bring them back from the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from Assyria I will gather them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the land of Gilead and Lebanon I will bring them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {room} will not be found for them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:11"/>And he will pass through the sea {of} distress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will strike the waves in the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the depths of the Nile will dry up.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And the pride of Assyria will be brought down,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the scepter of Egypt will depart.
<verse eid="ZEC 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 10:12"/>And I will strengthen them in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in his name they will walk”—
</para>
  <para style="q1">the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 10:12"/><verse eid="ZEC 10:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ZEC 11"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:1"/>Open your doors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lebanon, that fire may devour among your cedars!
<verse eid="ZEC 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:2"/>Wail, cypress, for the cedar has fallen, because the majestic ones have been devastated!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wail, oaks of Bashan, for the fortified forest has gone down.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:3"/>The voice of the wailing of the shepherds, for their glory is devastated!
</para>
  <para style="q1">The voice of the roaring of the young lions, for the pride of the Jordan is devastated!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:4"/>Thus says Yahweh my God, “Shepherd the flock of slaughter
<verse eid="ZEC 11:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:5"/>which the buyers kill and are not held guilty, and the ones selling them say, ‘Blessed be Yahweh, for I have become rich!’ And their shepherds do not pity them.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:6"/>Certainly I will no longer pity the inhabitants of the land”—the declaration of Yahweh—“and behold, I am causing mankind to fall, each man, in the hand of his neighbor and in the hand of his king, and they will crush the land, and I will not deliver {them} from their hand.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:7"/>And I shepherded the flock of slaughter, therefore the poor of the flock. And I took for myself two staffs. For the one I called “Favor,” and for the other I called “Union,” and I shepherded the flock.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:8"/>And I destroyed the three shepherds in one month.

</para>
  <para style="p">And my soul became short with them, and also their soul loathed me.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:9"/>And I said, “I will not shepherd you. The one dying, let it die, and the one being destroyed, let it be destroyed, and the ones remaining, let them eat, each one, the flesh of her companion.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:10"/>And I took my staff Favor, and I chopped it up, to break my covenant that I had cut with all the peoples.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:11"/>And it was broken on that day, and so the poor ones of the flock, the ones watching me, knew that it was the word of Yahweh.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:12"/>And I said to them,
“If it is good in your eyes, give my wages; but if not, refrain.” And they weighed out my wages, thirty
{pieces} of silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:13"/>And Yahweh said to me,
“Throw it to the potter, the magnificence of the price at which I was valued by them!” And I took the thirty {pieces} of silver and threw it
{into} the house of Yahweh, to the potter.
<verse eid="ZEC 11:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:14"/>And I chopped up my second staff, Union, to break the brotherhood between Judah and between Israel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:14"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:15"/>And Yahweh said to me,
“Again, take for yourself the equipment of a foolish shepherd,
<verse eid="ZEC 11:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:16"/>for behold, I am raising up a shepherd in the land. He will not attend to the ones being destroyed; he will not seek the scattered one; and he will not heal the broken one; he will not sustain the one standing; but he will eat the flesh of the fat one, and he will tear off their hooves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 11:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ZEC 11:17"/>Woe, worthless shepherd,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one forsaking the flock!
</para>
  <para style="q1">A sword against his arm and against his right eye!
</para>
  <para style="q1">His arm withering will wither, and his right eye dimming will dim!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 11:17"/><verse eid="ZEC 11:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ZEC 12"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:1"/>The burden of the word of Yahweh concerning Israel—the declaration of Yahweh, the one stretching out the heavens and founding the earth and forming the spirit of man within him.

<verse eid="ZEC 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:2"/>“Behold, I am making Jerusalem a cup of staggering for all of the peoples all around. And also against Judah it will be, in the siege against Jerusalem.
<verse eid="ZEC 12:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:3"/>And it will be on that day, I will make Jerusalem a stone of burden for all of the peoples. All of the ones lifting it, injuring, will be injured, and all of the nations of the earth will be gathered against it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 12:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:4"/>On that day”—the declaration of Yahweh—“I will strike every horse with confusion and its rider with madness. But over the house of Judah I will open my eyes, and every horse of the peoples I will strike with blindness.
<verse eid="ZEC 12:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:5"/>And the chiefs of Judah will say in their heart, ‘The inhabitants of Jerusalem are a strength to me by Yahweh of Armies, their God.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 12:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:6"/>On that day I will make the chiefs of Judah like a basin of fire among trees and like a torch of fire in a sheaf, and they will devour on the right and on the left all of the peoples all around. And Jerusalem will dwell again in its place, in Jerusalem.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:7"/>And Yahweh will save the tents of Judah at the first, so that the honor of the house of David and the honor of the dweller of Jerusalem will not be great over Judah.
<verse eid="ZEC 12:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:8"/>On that day Yahweh will defend on behalf of the inhabitant of Jerusalem, and the stumbler among them on that day will be like David, and the house of David, like God, like the angel of Yahweh to their face.

<verse eid="ZEC 12:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:9"/>“And it will be on that day, I will seek to destroy all of the nations coming against Jerusalem.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 12:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:10"/>And I will pour out on the house of David and on the inhabitant of Jerusalem a spirit of favor and supplications, and they will look to me, whom they pierced. And they will mourn over him as the mourning over the only one, and they will be bitter over him as being bitter over the firstborn.”
<verse eid="ZEC 12:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:11"/>On that day the mourning in Jerusalem will be great, like the mourning of Hadad Rimmon in the plain of Megiddo.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 12:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:12"/>And the land will mourn, clans, clans separately: the clan of the house of David separately, and their wives separately; the clan of the house of Nathan separately, and their wives separately,
<verse eid="ZEC 12:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:13"/>the clan of the house of Levi separately and their wives separately, the clan of the Shimeite separately and their wives separately,
<verse eid="ZEC 12:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 12:14"/>all of the clans, the ones remaining, clans, clans separately, and their wives separately.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 12:14"/><verse eid="ZEC 12:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="ZEC 13"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:1"/>On that day a fountain will be opened for the house of David and for the dwellers of Jerusalem, for sin and for impurity.
<verse eid="ZEC 13:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:2"/>“And it will happen on that day”—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—“I will cut off the names of the idols from the land, and they will not be remembered again, and also I will cause the prophets and the spirit of uncleanness to pass from the land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:3"/>And it will happen, when a man prophesies again, then his father and his mother, the ones bearing him, will say to him,
‘You will not live, for you have spoken falsehood in the name of Yahweh.’ And his father and his mother, the ones bearing him, will pierce him in his prophesying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:4"/>And it will happen on that day, the prophets will have shame, each man from his vision, in his prophesying. And they will not wear a cloak of hair in order to deceive.
<verse eid="ZEC 13:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:5"/>And he will say, ‘I am not a prophet. I am a man working the ground, for a man has owned me from my youth.’
<verse eid="ZEC 13:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:6"/>And {someone} will say to him, ‘What are these wounds between your hands?’ And he will say, ‘Those are the ones with which I was struck {in} the house of my lovers.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 13:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:7"/>Sword, awake against my shepherd,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and against the man, my companion”—the declaration of Yahweh of Armies—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Strike the shepherd,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the flock will scatter,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will turn my hand against the little ones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 13:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:8"/>And it will happen in all the land”—the declaration of Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q2">“two portions in it will be cut off, they will expire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the third will be left in it.
<verse eid="ZEC 13:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 13:9"/>And I will bring the third into the fire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will refine them as
{one} refines the silver,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will test them as
{one} tests the gold.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He, he will call on my name,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I, I will answer him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will say,
‘He is my people,’
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he, he will say,
‘Yahweh is my God.’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ZEC 13:9"/><verse eid="ZEC 13:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="ZEC 14"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:1"/>Behold, a day is coming for Yahweh, and your spoil will be divided in your midst.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:2"/>“And I will gather all the nations to Jerusalem for the battle, and the city will be captured, and the houses will be plundered, and the women will be raped. And half of the city will go out into the exile, but the rest of the people will not be cut off from the city.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:3"/>And Yahweh will go out and will fight against those nations, like the day of his fighting on a day of battle.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:4"/>And his feet will stand on that day on the Mount of Olives, which is on the face of Jerusalem from the east. And the Mount of Olives will be split from its half toward the east and toward the west, a very great valley. And half of the mountain will move away toward the north, and its half toward the south.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:5"/>And you will flee {by} the valley of my mountains, for the valley of the mountains will reach to Azal. And you will flee just as you fled from the face of the earthquake in the days of Uzziah the king of Judah. And Yahweh my God will come, all the holy ones with you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:6"/>And it will happen on that day, there will not be light; the splendid will congeal.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:7"/>And it will be one day—it, it will be known to Yahweh—not day and not night. And it will happen, at the time of evening there will be light.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:8"/>And it will happen on that day, living waters will go out from Jerusalem, half of them to the eastern sea and half of them to the western sea; it will happen in the summer and in the winter.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:9"/>And Yahweh will be as king over all the earth. On that day Yahweh will be one, and his name, one.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:10"/>All the land will turn like the Arabah from Geba to Rimmon, south of Jerusalem. But it will rise up and will dwell in its place from the Gate of Benjamin to the place of the First Gate, to the Gate of the Corners, and {from} the Tower of Hananel to the winepresses of the king.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:11"/>And they will dwell in it, and there will not again be destruction; and Jerusalem will dwell in security.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:12"/>And this will be the plague with which Yahweh will strike all the peoples who waged war against Jerusalem: his flesh will rot away while he is standing on his feet, and his eyes will rot in their sockets, and his tongue will rot in their mouth.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:13"/>And it will happen on that day, a great tumult of Yahweh will be among them, and each man will seize the hand of his neighbor, and his hand will go up against the hand of his neighbor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:14"/>And also Judah will fight at Jerusalem. And the wealth of all the nations around will be gathered—gold and silver and garments in very great abundance.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:15"/>And thus will be the plague of the horse, the mule, the camel, and the donkey, and every beast that will be in those camps, like this plague.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:16"/>And it will happen, everyone remaining from all the nations, the ones coming against Jerusalem, will go up as often as year by year to bow down to the King, Yahweh of Armies, and to celebrate the Festival of Booths.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:17"/>And it will happen, whoever does not go up from the clans of the earth to Jerusalem to bow down to the King, Yahweh of Armies—on them there will not be the rain.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:17"/><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:18"/>And if the clan of Egypt does not go up and does not come, then not on them. There will be the plague with which Yahweh strikes the nations that do not go up to celebrate the Festival of Booths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:19"/>This will be the sin of Egypt and the sin of all the nations that do not go up to celebrate the Festival of Booths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ZEC 14:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:20"/>On that day there will be on the bells of the horse,
“Holy to Yahweh.” And the pots in the house of Yahweh will be like the bowls to the face of the altar.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:20"/><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ZEC 14:21"/>And every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah will be holy to Yahweh of Armies, and all the ones sacrificing will come and will take from them and will boil in them. And there will not be a Canaanite again in the house of Yahweh of Armies on that day.
<verse eid="ZEC 14:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ZEC 14"/>
</usx>
